# Python Environment

## Virtual Environment

- The project uses a virtual environment at `/home/marco/venv/`
- Always activate it before running any Python commands: `source /home/marco/venv/bin/activate`
- After activation, use `python` (not `python3`) to run scripts
- The venv contains all project dependencies: PyTorch, OpenCV, pypdfium2, transformers, EasyOCR, etc.

## Running Scripts

- Activate the venv first, then run from the project root:
  ```
  source /home/marco/venv/bin/activate
  python DevEnv/SomeScript.py
  ```
- If the venv is already activated in the current shell session, do not re-activate it
